- All file modifications must preserve UTF-8 encoding.
- Never replace non-ASCII characters with garbled text or placeholder symbols.

# Strict Encoding Rules
NEVER write, edit, or modify any file using system default encodings like CP437 or Windows-1252.
ALWAYS explicitly read and save files using strictly UTF-8 encoding.
If modifying text containing corrupt characters like 'ΓÇö', you MUST immediately clean them up and replace them with a proper em dash '—'.
